<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The Argon2id password hashing surface targets all three LTS/STS lines.
         The PostQuantum.Jwt hybrid-token integration is net10.0-only because the
         BCL post-quantum primitives (ML-DSA/ML-KEM) and PostQuantum.Jwt itself
         ship for .NET 10. That code is gated behind #if NET10_0_OR_GREATER and a
         conditional package reference — see Tokens/ and KNOWN-GAPS.md. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>PostQuantum.Identity</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>PostQuantum.Identity</AssemblyName>
    <!-- The net10 token surface serializes claims via source-generated
         JsonTypeInfo<T> (PostQuantumIdentityJsonContext) and PostQuantum.Jwt's
         typed WithClaim<T> overload, so it is trim/AOT-clean. The Argon2id path
         (Konscious + Identity.Core) raises no trim warnings for our usage either.
         Asserted on net10 only — the trim/AOT analyzers ship with that SDK band. -->
    <IsAotCompatible Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet package metadata -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>PostQuantum.Identity</PackageId>
    <Version>0.5.0-preview.1</Version>
    <Title>PostQuantum.Identity — post-quantum ASP.NET Core Identity</Title>
    <Authors>Paul Clark</Authors>
    <Description>Post-quantum integration for ASP.NET Core Identity, with two surfaces at deliberately different maturity profiles. (1) PRODUCTION-READY Argon2id password hashing — PHC-formatted, secure-by-default work factors, transparent rehash-on-login, one-line PBKDF2→Argon2id migration via AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration, fail-closed verification, RFC 9106 §5.3 Known Answer Tests + reference-CLI PHC interop + emitter wire-format pin. Runs on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. (2) PREVIEW hybrid post-quantum JWT issuance for owned/trusted ecosystems — ML-DSA-65 signatures (FIPS 204) with optional X-Wing (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) encryption, kid-based key rotation, JSON-source-gen claim path. Uses non-IANA algorithm identifiers; intentionally not interoperable with generic JWT tooling. Requires .NET 10 (and OpenSSL 3.5+ on Linux). Supply chain: every .nupkg ships with an embedded CycloneDX SBOM, GitHub Sigstore-signed build-provenance attestation (verifiable with gh attestation verify), deterministic SourceLink builds, .snupkg symbols, CodeQL on every PR, Dependabot. Not yet independently audited. See https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity for the production-readiness stance, the Roadmap to 1.0, the migration guide, and runnable minimal-API + MVC samples.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>aspnetcore;identity;aspnet-identity;password-hashing;argon2;argon2id;phc;owasp;jwt;jwt-token;post-quantum;pqc;quantum-resistant;ml-dsa;ml-kem;x-wing;hybrid-cryptography;authentication;cryptography;security;fips-204;sbom;cyclonedx;net8;net9;net10</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
0.5.0-preview.1 — Final production-readiness polish. No public API changes; no behavior changes.

Positioning:
  - README leads with an explicit "Production-ready for owned and trusted
    ecosystems" banner above the split-surface maturity table.
  - "Roadmap to 1.0" gates re-framed as external-signal blockers (upstream
    PostQuantum.Jwt 1.0, IETF JOSE PQC drafts, third-party audit) rather
    than missing engineering — the version label is conservative on
    purpose, the code beneath is production-discipline.
  - SECURITY.md and KNOWN-GAPS.md honesty statements re-aligned to match.

Supply chain:
  - README's verification section renamed "How to verify this package
    (supply chain — three commands)" so it is easy to find for auditors
    landing on the page cold.
  - New docs/SUPPLY-CHAIN.md — auditor-facing companion: chain-of-custody
    diagram, per-arrow verification table, full release.yml hygiene
    checklist, reproducibility recipe, SHA-256 cross-check guidance, and
    a "what this does NOT prove" honesty section.

Reference samples:
  - PostQuantum.Identity.Mvc.Demo: token Lifetime lifted into a single
    TokenConstants.Lifetime source-of-truth; AccountController login and
    refresh responses now surface expires_in for parity with the
    minimal-API demo.

Repo hygiene:
  - .gitignore now explicitly excludes nuget.key / nuget.key.* / *.nuget.key
    so a stray local API-key file at the repo root can never be committed.

Earlier highlights — 0.3.0 added hardened Argon2id and token KATs, the
production-shaped samples (refresh/logout/JWKS/revocation), opinionated
work-factor presets, startup options validation, the preflight logger, and
the supply-chain verification flow. 0.2.0 added the PBKDF2→Argon2id
migrating hasher, kid rotation, AOT-clean claim path, embedded CycloneDX
SBOM, CI/release workflows, and benchmarks.

Still preview — NOT independently audited. See KNOWN-GAPS.md.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Paul Clark</Copyright>
    <NeutralLanguage>en-US</NeutralLanguage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Symbols + SourceLink for debuggable, reproducible packages. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Argon2id implementation (Argon2 1.3 spec, PHC winner). Used on every TFM. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Konscious.Security.Cryptography.Argon2" Version="1.3.1" />
    <!-- Framework-agnostic ASP.NET Core Identity core: IPasswordHasher<TUser>,
         PasswordHasher<TUser>, IdentityBuilder, UserManager<TUser>. No EF / web host pulled in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Core" Version="10.0.9" />
    <!-- For the opt-in AddPostQuantumPreflightLogging() hosted service. The
         abstractions package keeps the dep surface tiny — no full host runtime
         pulled in for callers who never opt in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Hybrid-token integration: PostQuantum.Jwt + BCL PQC ship for .NET 10 only. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="PostQuantum.Jwt" Version="1.0.0-preview.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Generate a CycloneDX SBOM (bom.json) inside the package on every Pack.
       Requires the `dotnet-CycloneDX` global tool (one-time install via
       `dotnet tool install` with the `global` flag and id `CycloneDX`). If the
       tool isn't present (e.g. a fresh dev machine), pack continues without the
       SBOM rather than failing; the release workflow installs the tool
       unconditionally, so CI always produces the SBOM.

       The bom.json is added via an in-target ItemGroup because
       $(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json doesn't exist when a static <None Include>
       would be evaluated. Pinned to the net10.0 graph so the tool runs once. -->
  <Target Name="GenerateCycloneDxSbom"
          BeforeTargets="GenerateNuspec;_GetPackageFiles"
          Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false' and '$(SbomDisabled)' != 'true'">
    <!-- IMPORTANT: the disable-package-restore flag is required. CycloneDX
         otherwise runs its own restore, and on a multi-targeted project that
         rewrites obj/project.assets.json to a single TFM, which then collapses
         the per-TFM dependency groups in the generated .nuspec (NU5128) and would
         drop transitive deps for net8.0/net9.0 consumers. With restore disabled
         it reads the existing multi-TFM assets and aggregates all frameworks. -->
    <Exec Command="dotnet CycloneDX &quot;$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)&quot; --disable-package-restore --output &quot;$(IntermediateOutputPath.TrimEnd('\').TrimEnd('/'))&quot; --filename bom.json --json"
          IgnoreExitCode="true"
          ContinueOnError="WarnAndContinue">
      <Output TaskParameter="ExitCode" PropertyName="_CycloneDxExitCode" />
    </Exec>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM not generated (tool missing or failed, exit=$(_CycloneDxExitCode)). Install with: `dotnet tool install` (global, id=CycloneDX)."
             Condition="'$(_CycloneDxExitCode)' != '0'" />
    <ItemGroup Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')">
      <None Include="$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM packed into .nupkg at /bom.json"
             Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')" />
  </Target>

</Project>
